    "summary": "Wooden openwork lintel, pare, stained black. Three wheku figures, unsexed, with inlaid haliotis shell eyes, raised arms, surface decoration of spirals and pakura, separated and flanked by takarangi spirals. Solid base with bands of rauponga, central rauponga spiral and two terminal manaia with haliotis-shell eyes under feet of outer wheku figures.",
